00a46687d30","file":"preprints/The-Sharp-Logarithmic-Exponent-of-r-5-t-September-24-2026/build/introduction.tex","line":11,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"2c4c369cf3aa67173a442d69946f181c7f3847140e8c5dc0136cd220ab264c5e","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/The-Sharp-Logarithmic-Exponent-of-r-5-t-September-24-2026/build/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:8f02cb89aef0c3ff2d30b491d7810e72fdbbf28f0b92b3199625300a46687d30","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/The-Sharp-Logarithmic-Exponent-of-r-5-t-September-24-2026/build/introduction.tex#L11"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nThere is an absolute constant \\(C>0\\) such that, for every\n\\(\\varepsilon>0\\), all sufficiently large integers \\(t\\) satisfy\n\\[\n \\frac{t^4}{(\\log t)^{3+\\varepsilon}}\n \\ \\le\\ r(5,t)\\ \\le\\\n C\\frac{t^4}{(\\log t)^3}.\n\\]\nThe threshold for \\(t\\) may depend on \\(\\varepsilon\\).\nConsequently,\n\\[\n \\lim_{t\\to\\infty}\n \\frac{4\\log t-\\log r(5,t)}{\\log\\log t}=3.\n\\]"}
